# Binance.Net in this repo

Treat **[Binance.Net](https://github.com/JKorf/Binance.Net)** as the **framework** for Binance-facing .NET code: `IBinanceRestClient` / `IBinanceSocketClient`, USD-M Futures APIs under `UsdFuturesApi`, and **models as returned by the API** (e.g. `BinanceFuturesUsdtSymbol`, filters, klines). Prefer library types and client methods over re-modeling exchange payloads unless the code is translating **into Platform Domain** or **through Application interfaces** (there use domain types).

## Where this applies

- **Platform Infrastructure** (MarketData, Execution): primary home for clients, options, and Binance-specific logic.
- **Legacy monolith** (`src/legacy/TradingAssistant/TradingAssistant/BinanceService.cs`): direct Binance.Net usage; use `BinanceCredentials` (12.11+).
- **Backtesting MVP** (`src/mvp/Backtesting/`): isolated tools may reference Binance.Net directly for klines, `KlineInterval`, exchange info, and filters.
- **WebSocketTrading MVP** (`src/mvp/WebSocketTrading/`): live Worker; REST warmup/account setup + WS kline stream + WS API orders. Pins Binance.Net **13.1.1** (MVP-only).

## Where it does not

- **Platform Domain and Application** must remain **free of Binance.Net in public contracts**. Adapters in Infrastructure translate Binance.Net models to domain types.

## Practices

- Use official client surfaces (`ExchangeData`, `Account`, etc.) and **CryptoExchange.Net** patterns consistent with existing `BinanceService` code.
- Keep **version alignment**: Platform and legacy use the **same** Binance.Net version (12.11.x). WebSocketTrading MVP is an exception (13.1.1).
